**Pitfall: Single Page Application (SPA) 404 Routing Error:**
If you use client-side routers (like React Router) and deploy to Cloudflare Pages, navigating directly to a deep URL like `https://app.pages.dev/dashboard` results in a `404 Not Found` error. This happens because the Cloudflare Edge looks for a physical file named `dashboard.html`.
**Fix**: Create a `_redirects` file in your `public/` directory:
\begin{lstlisting}
/* /index.html 200
\end{lstlisting}
This tells the edge server to rewrite all incoming routes to `index.html` with an HTTP 200 status, allowing client-side JavaScript to handle the routing seamlessly!
